invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's general Jacobian addition runs its formula on
  a running sum at infinity. The sum's coordinates are then zero, U1 and
  S1 are zero, the formula takes the case of two equal points and doubles
  the zero point, so the first multiple of the key the pass adds is lost
  whenever no multiple of G came before it. bin/p256_verify_equiv_test
  requires the 32-bit verifier's verdict on every signature it tries.

--- old
    if (p256_wide_jacobian_is_infinity(a)) {
        *o = *b;
        return;
    }
--- new
